-- Durotar (zone 14): remove doubled holiday spawns (seen only during Noblegarden and Midsummer).
--
-- 1) Noblegarden, Razor Hill: the eggs were imported twice. 61 egg spots carry a pool of four Brightly Colored Eggs
--    (113769-113772, pool max 1: one egg per spot), and a second, unpooled import (guids 210xxx-212xxx and a few older
--    ones) put four or five more eggs of all colours on most of the same spots, and on nine spots of its own (eight of
--    them with several eggs). During Noblegarden a player saw a stack of eggs on one spot. AzerothCore's Noblegarden has
--    one egg per spot (e.g. 113772 at 273.9,-4729.5, the same spot as pool 13937); neither TDB has Noblegarden eggs in
--    Durotar.
--    The dossier counted 123 (the draft's header 122) doubles of the SAME entry within 0.5 yd; settled: 123 same-entry
--    pairs (122 pooled+unpooled, one unpooled pair), but the real stacks hold every colour, so the rule here is wider:
--    delete every unpooled egg standing within 1 yd of a pooled egg, and on the unpooled-only spots keep the lowest guid
--    and delete the rest. One of those spots, 303.1,-4648.7 (egg 210223 and trap 210224), is 2.1 yd from pooled spot
--    13921 (trap 9780 at 303.1,-4646.6, where the second import's own trap 210039 stood doubled): taken as the same spot
--    imported 2 yd off, so its last egg and its trap go too. The next nearest unpooled-only spot is 4.6 yd from a pool:
--    those are kept as separate spots. The other traps (one per spot of the second import, size 0.1, radius 0) are left.
--    187 objects: 185 eggs and 2 traps. Kept: 61 pooled spots and 8 unpooled eggs. Nothing references them but
--    their event rows (game_event 9). Ours: the 1 yd rule, the 2.1 yd spot and which copy is kept.
-- 2) Midsummer, Razor Hill Outskirts: the camp was imported twice on identical spots (353xxx/195xxx-196xxx and
--    369xxx/213xxx, both tied to event 1). Delete the second copy: Midsummer Celebrants 16781 x4, Midsummer Bonfire 16592,
--    Flame Eater 25994, [DND] Midsummer Bonfire Faction Bunny 26355, and objects 181355 x3, 188021, 181307, 181305.
--    Neither TDB has this camp; the camp itself is kept. A stacked pair of 181300 "Standing, Large - MFF" lights at the
--    blockade (195987/195989) differs in height and facing, a deliberate decoration: kept.

